SIX VERDICTS PASS AND FOUR FAIL. The four failures are TWO defects, NEITHER of them D-C5 or
D-C8, and both reported as failures with nothing relaxed:

  (1) The greedy and T=0.02 residuals on Qwen are MEASURED bfloat16 ties.
      logs/d11_greedy_tie_probe.log runs the gate case's own _load/_paged_config/
      _distinct_rows, the same tokens=[1]*32, positions=[128]*32 and the gate's exact
      T=0.02 policy, and prints the top-two gap per slot on the composed float32 logits:
        slot  4: gap=0   p(runner-up)@temp50=0.5
        slot 12: gap=0   p(runner-up)@temp50=0.5
        slot 21: gap=0   p(runner-up)@temp50=0.5
        the-32-smallest-gaps=[4, 12, 21, 10, 28, 5, 14, 3, ...]
      EXACTLY THREE Qwen slots have a top-two gap of zero - two ids attaining the row maximum
      in bfloat16 - and they are 4, 12 and 21. The gate misses [4, 21], byte-identically in
      three fresh processes. torch.argmax breaks a zero gap by lowest index; a sampler drawing
      from a softmax has a 50% chance either way. Two of the three zero-gap slots disagreeing,
      one agreeing, and no fourth slot to explain, is what a tie looks like. The greedy claim's
      single residual is the same slot 4, measured directly in the same log:
        [tie] slot 4: host 16 @ 15.375  device 17 @ 15.375  equal=True  gap=0.0
              ids sharing the row maximum=2
      The claim as WORDED (32/32) is still not met and nothing was relaxed to make it met.
      Llama's [2, 11] gaps are measured by tie_llama_r1-r3 (attempt 9's q17).

  (2) The two seeded-slot failures are D-C12 - see the D-C12 entry in REPORT.md.

A CORRECTION THIS ATTEMPT FORCES, recorded because the previous reading is in this report:
  The near-zero-temperature test's call order is decode_logits (no sampling), then
  cold = decode_sampled(T=0.02), then hot = decode_sampled(T=2.0). `hot` is the SECOND device
  sampling call in the process, which is exactly what D-C12 corrupts. The same structure in
  d11_greedy_tie_probe.log fails the same way: its first-call [tie] half is sane, its
  second-call [cold] half reports missed=True in ALL 32 slots with device ids like 3212836881
  and 1077395535 - float32 bit patterns, not tokens.
  So "T=2.0 agrees 0/32" is NOT evidence about the reciprocal-temperature convention, and the
  earlier "D4 is confirmed twice" reading is withdrawn. D4 IS still confirmed, on the T=0.02
  direction alone, and that direction suffices: under the inverted convention the distribution
  is near-uniform over 32 candidates, so 30 of 32 slots landing on the argmax is a ~1/32**30
  event.

D-C2 (per-request vs per-(request, slot) seeding) IS RECORDED AND NOT CHANGED, as the brief
requires. Current behaviour, read off models/common/modules/sampling/sampling_2d.py:742-752:

  def _seed_digest(seed, slot, *, bits):
      payload = f"sampling2d:{seed}:{slot}".encode("ascii")
      return int.from_bytes(hashlib.blake2b(payload, digest_size=8).digest(), "little") & ((1 << bits) - 1)
  def _device_seed(seed, slot):  return _seed_digest(seed, slot, bits=31)
  def _host_seed(seed, slot):    return _seed_digest(seed, slot, bits=63)

So TODAY THE SEED IS PER-(REQUEST, SLOT): the blake2b payload contains both the request seed
and the slot index, so the same request seed gives 32 different device streams. Device and host
share the payload and differ only in the truncation width (31 vs 63 bits), so a device stream
and a host stream at the same seed are NOT expected to match token for token - which is why the
step-7 brief says a seeded device-vs-host comparison cannot be the D4 check.
Nothing about any of this was changed by this job, per the brief.
